  7. AUDIBILITY OF THE FILTER-REBUILD PATCH
     Identical 16.85 kHz input and identical ratio schedule through the gated
     and ungated code, sample for sample. The ratio sweeps +/-50 ppm and
     crosses 1.0, so WDL's 3% guard-band low-pass switches in and out during
     the run -- the one moment a coefficient change could be heard.

     rebuilds, gated   : 3
     rebuilds, ungated : 275
     difference        : -148.3 dB relative to signal, peak 1.79E-007

     PASS - the gate moves the output ~20 dB below the resampler's own error floor.

